title: "Start Device Authorization"
icon: arrow-up-right
description: "Start Device Authorization: deviceAuthorize in the TypeScript, Python and Rust clients."
---

`POST /v1/auth/device/code`

Starts the device authorization flow for a CLI or another device without a browser. Show the verification URL and user code, then poll the token endpoint at the returned interval. No request fields are required; any supplied body is ignored.

<Tabs>
<Tab title="TypeScript">
```typescript TypeScript
photon.auth.device.authorize(input?: DeviceAuthorizeInput, options?: RequestOptions): Promise<DeviceAuthorizeOutput>
```
</Tab>
<Tab title="Python">
```python Python
photon.auth.device.authorize(input: DeviceAuthorizeInput | None = None) -> models.DeviceAuthorizeResponse
```
</Tab>
<Tab title="Rust">
```rust Rust
client.device_authorize().await -> Result<ResponseValue<types::DeviceAuthorizeResponse>, Error<DeviceAuthorizeError>>
```
</Tab>
</Tabs>

<RequestExample>
```typescript TypeScript
import { Photon } from "@photon-ai/api";

const photon = new Photon();
const result = await photon.auth.device.authorize();
```

```python Python
from photon_api import Photon

photon = Photon()
result = photon.auth.device.authorize()
```

```rust Rust
use photon_ai_api::PhotonClientBuilder;

let client = PhotonClientBuilder::new().build()?;
let result = client
    .device_authorize()
    .await
    .map_err(|error| format!("{error:?}"))?
    .into_inner();
```

</RequestExample>

<ResponseExample>
```json 200
{
  "device_code": "string",
  "expires_in": 0,
  "interval": 0,
  "user_code": "string",
  "verification_uri": "string",
  "verification_uri_complete": "string"
}
```

</ResponseExample>

## Returns

**`200`** Verification details for the RFC 8628 device flow. The optional JSON or form body is ignored; the authorization client is selected by the server. DeviceAuthorizeResponse

<ResponseField name="device_code" type={"string"} required>
Opaque device code to exchange at POST /v1/auth/device/token while waiting for the user to authorize.
</ResponseField>

<ResponseField name="expires_in" type={"number"} required>
Lifetime of the device code and user code, in seconds.
</ResponseField>

<ResponseField name="interval" type={"number"} required>
Minimum number of seconds to wait between token polling requests.
</ResponseField>

<ResponseField name="user_code" type={"string"} required>
Code the user enters at verification_uri to authorize this device.
</ResponseField>

<ResponseField name="verification_uri" type={"string"} required>
Browser URL where the user enters user_code and authorizes the device.
</ResponseField>

<ResponseField name="verification_uri_complete" type={"string"} required>
Browser URL with user_code included, ready to open or encode as a QR code.
</ResponseField>

